# M0.6 (STRETCH) — MACE via the ML-IAP unified interface as a `pair_style
#        hybrid` sub-style with a NULL type map.
#
# UNDOCUMENTED TERRITORY — ANY FAILURE MODE IS A VALID *FAIL* RESULT.
# Nothing downstream depends on this deck. `pair_style mace` cannot NULL-map
# types (ACEsuit #1314), which is what confines MACE to full-cell runs. If
# `mliap unified` tolerates NULL inside `hybrid`, MACE gains partial-cell
# coverage and the capability matrix's row-2/row-3 MACE cells change from No to
# Conditional. If it segfaults, errors, or silently produces wrong energies,
# record that and move on — the DeePMD partial-cell path is unaffected.
#
# Geometry: trilayer_mos2.data from make_geometries.py — 36 atoms, 6 atom types,
# the same file M0.1 uses, so the two are directly comparable.
# TYPE LAYOUT:
#   1 = Mo layer 1   2 = S layer 1
#   3 = Mo layer 2   4 = S layer 2
#   5 = Mo layer 3   6 = S layer 3
#
# Layout mirrors M0.1, with ONE mliap instance covering layer 1 only and lj/cut
# supplying everything else. A single instance is deliberate: repeated `mliap`
# sub-styles in one hybrid is a further step into undocumented behaviour and is
# only worth trying if this deck passes.
#
# Model: produced by `mace_create_lammps_model --format=mliap` (see
# documentation/milestone0.md). The trailing `0` is the ghost-neighbour flag.
#
# Run:  $PREFIX/lammps-mace/build/lmp -k on g 1 -sf kk -in m0_6_mliap_hybrid.in

units metal
atom_style atomic
read_data trilayer_mos2.data
pair_style hybrid mliap unified mace-mliap_lammps.pt 0 lj/cut 11.0
pair_coeff * * mliap Mo S NULL NULL NULL NULL
pair_coeff 1*2 3*6 lj/cut 0.0224 3.13   # layer1 <-> layers 2,3
pair_coeff 3*6 3*6 lj/cut 0.0224 3.13   # everything not covered by mliap
# Masses are also in the data file; repeated here so the deck is self-contained.
mass 1 95.95   # Mo
mass 2 32.06   # S
mass 3 95.95   # Mo
mass 4 32.06   # S
mass 5 95.95   # Mo
mass 6 32.06   # S
thermo 1
run 0
fix nve all nve
run 20
